# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored -- see .gitignore's `*.local`
# pattern) and fill in a value for local development.
#
# VITE_DEV_AUTH_TOKEN authenticates frontend API requests against the
# backend's ServiceCredential dependency (api/dependencies.py::get_current_user).
# Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed variable into the built client-side JS
# bundle -- anyone who can load the page can read it back out. That makes
# this variable unsafe for a real ServiceCredential (especially an admin
# one, e.g. from `lead-harvester issue-service-credential`): it would ship
# a working bearer token to every browser that loads the frontend, dev
# build or not.
#
# Set DEV_AUTH_ENABLED=true (and DEV_AUTH_USER, optionally) on your own
# local backend instead -- Settings refuses to allow that flag outside
# development/test (config.py), so it can't leak into a real deployment --
# and leave this variable unset. It exists only in case a future
# interactive user/session login flow needs a short-lived token here; do
# not put a long-lived service credential in it.
VITE_DEV_AUTH_TOKEN=
